COMMAND NAME: mppactivatestandby.sh

Activates the backup master as the active MPP master instance 
for a Bizgres MPP system.


*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppactivatestandby.sh -d <standby_master_datadir> [-f] [-a] [-q] 
[-l <logfile_directory>]

mppactivatestandby.sh [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppactivatestandby.sh script activates a backup master host 
and brings it into operation as the primary master instance for a 
Bizgres MPP system. You must run this script from the backup master 
host you are activating, not the failed primary master host. Running 
this script assumes you have a backup master host configured for the 
system (see mppinitstandby.sh).

The script will perform the following steps:

* Stop the snchronization process (mppsyncmaster) on the backup master

* Update the system catalog tables of the backup master using the logs

* Activate the backup master to be the new primary master for the system

* Restart the Bizgres MPP system with the new master host

A backup MPP master host serves as a `warm standby' in the event of the 
primary MPP master host becoming unoperational. The backup master is 
kept up to date by a transaction log replication process (mppsyncmaster), 
which runs on the backup master host and keeps the data between the primary 
and backup master hosts synchronized. 

If the primary master fails, the log replication process is shutdown, 
and the backup master can be activated in its place by using the 
mppactivatestandby.sh script. Upon activation of the backup master, the 
replicated logs are used to reconstruct the state of the MPP master host 
at the time of the last successfully committed transaction. To reactivate 
the original primary master host, use the mppactivatemaster.sh script.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-d <standby_master_datadir>

Required. The absolute path of the data directory on the backup 
master host.

-f

Use this option to force activation of the backup master host when the 
synchronization process (mppsyncmaster) is not running. Only use this 
option if you are sure that the backup and primary master hosts are 
consistent, and you know the mppsyncmaster process is not running on the 
backup master host. This option may be useful if you have just initialized 
a new backup master using mppinitstandby.sh, and want to activate it 
immediately.

-a

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.

-q

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, but is 
still written to the log file.

-l logfile_directory

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Activate the backup master host and make it the active master instance 
for a Bizgres MPP system (run from backup master host you are activating):

mppactivatestandby.sh -d /mppdata


